<mxCell id="b7" value="7" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#0288D1;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1000" y="55" width="36" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="b8" value="8" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#F4B400;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1690" y="180" width="36" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="b9" value="9" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#00897B;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="870" y="435" width="36" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="b10" value="10" style="ellipse;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;aspect=fixed;fillColor=#00897B;strokeColor=none;fontColor=#ffffff;fontStyle=1;fontSize=15;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1000" y="30" width="36" height="36" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
<mxCell id="note" value="&lt;b&gt;Yes — this chain works, with one control added at hop 7:&lt;/b&gt; the Node.js Writer must accept calls &lt;u&gt;only&lt;/u&gt; from the Write-back API&#39;s service account (Workload Identity ID-token or mTLS, plus a NetworkPolicy allowing ingress only from the gatekeeper pod). Otherwise anything inside the network could call the writer and bypass steps 4–6.&#10;&lt;b&gt;Division of responsibility:&lt;/b&gt; Write-back API = trust decisions (Looker signature, user step-up via Apigee→ID&amp;A, tenant policy). Node.js Writer = data operation only (Google&#39;s reference: Storage Write API append, runtime SA scoped to the tenant dataset). Two APIs, two owners, two blast radii. Synchronous end-to-end: Looker gets 200 within the request." style="text;html=1;fontSize=12;align=left;spacing=10;fillColor=#FDECEA;strokeColor=#EA4335;rounded=1;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="60" y="660" width="1980" height="110" as="geometry"/></mxCell>
</root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
</mxfile>